---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Solving Quadratic Equations by Factorisation | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to solve quadratic equations by factorisation and splitting the middle term with step-by-step examples for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/quadratic-equations" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Quadratic Equations</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">02</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 02 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS</div>
					<h1>Solving by <span>Factorisation</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master the method of splitting the middle term to factorise quadratic expressions and find their roots easily.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · CONCEPT -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE CONCEPT</div>
					<h2>Splitting the Middle Term</h2>
					<p>
						To factorise <em>ax² + bx + c = 0</em>, we find two numbers <strong>p</strong> and <strong>q</strong> such that:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>p + q = b &nbsp;and&nbsp; p × q = a × c</strong>
						<span>Splitting the middle term bx into px + qx allows grouping into two linear factors.</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">✓</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Zero Product Property</strong>
							<p>
								If <em>(x - α)(x - β) = 0</em>, then either <em>x - α = 0</em> or <em>x - β = 0</em>. Hence, <strong>x = α</strong> or <strong>x = β</strong> are the roots of the equation.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · STEP-BY-STEP EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Solved Practice Examples</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the roots of x² - 5x + 6 = 0</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Identify coefficients</strong>: a = 1, b = -5, c = 6. We need p × q = 6 and p + q = -5.</p>
							<p>The numbers are <strong>-2</strong> and <strong>-3</strong>.</p>
							<p><strong>Step 2: Split the middle term</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x² - 2x - 3x + 6 = 0<br/>
								x(x - 2) - 3(x - 2) = 0<br/>
								<strong>(x - 2)(x - 3) = 0</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 3: Equate factors to 0</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x - 2 = 0 ⟹ <strong>x = 2</strong><br/>
								x - 3 = 0 ⟹ <strong>x = 3</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;">Roots are <strong>x = 2</strong> and <strong>x = 3</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2</span>
							<h3>Find the roots of 2x² - x - 6 = 0</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>Step 1: Identify coefficients</strong>: a = 2, b = -1, c = -6. Product = a × c = 2 × (-6) = -12. We need p + q = -1.</p>
							<p>The numbers are <strong>-4</strong> and <strong>3</strong>.</p>
							<p><strong>Step 2: Split the middle term & factorise</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								2x² - 4x + 3x - 6 = 0<br/>
								2x(x - 2) + 3(x - 2) = 0<br/>
								<strong>(2x + 3)(x - 2) = 0</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:12px;"><strong>Step 3: Solve for x</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								2x + 3 = 0 ⟹ <strong>x = -3/2</strong><br/>
								x - 2 = 0 ⟹ <strong>x = 2</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Steps</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Find two numbers whose product is <strong>a × c</strong> and sum is <strong>b</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Rewrite the middle term <em>bx</em> using these two numbers and factorise by grouping.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Set each linear factor to zero to find the roots <strong>x = α</strong> and <strong>x = β</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/quadratic-equations/introduction" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Introduction to Quadratic Equations</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/quadratic-equations/completing-the-square" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Completing the Square</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">QUADRATIC EQUATIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 02 of 05</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 40%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/quadratic-equations/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction</strong>
									<small>Standard form & basics</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/factorisation" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Factorisation Method</strong>
									<small>Splitting the middle term</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/completing-the-square" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Completing the Square</strong>
									<small>Perfect square method</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/quadratic-formula" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Quadratic Formula</strong>
									<small>Formula & solutions</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/quadratic-equations/nature-of-roots" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>05</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Nature of Roots</strong>
									<small>Discriminant D = b² - 4ac</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

